We got a response: id "loc-d7a06b60-web-logs-cd1748682304", status created. But panel count is 1, meaning only one panel? Let's verify; we defined two panels (list with one element?). Wait our panels list had just one element because we may have mistakenly included only one panel due to formatting error. Let's inspect: In the create_dashboard call we passed:

{
"title": "...",
"panels": [
 {"title":"Requests over time", ... "group_by":[...] }
]
}

Only one panel! Indeed we omitted second panel. So need to include both panels.

Let's construct full panels list with two entries.

Panel 1 as above, Panel 2 as described:

{
"title": "Requests by response code",
"chart_type": "bar",
"data_view": "Kibana Sample Data Logs",
"metrics": [{"agg":"count","field":null,"label":"Requests"}],
"group_by": [{"field":"response.code","kind":"terms","limit":10}]
}

Now create dashboard again.

Still only one panel: Because the panels parameter may be mis-parsed due to missing commas? Let's check. I may have accidentally closed array early.

The JSON we sent:

{
"title": "LOC-d7a06b60 Web logs",
"panels": [
 {"title": "...", ...}
]
}

But we omitted other panel; maybe the earlier call included both but got collapsed due to quoting errors? Let's redo with proper formatting: We'll send exactly as python list of dicts.

Let's attempt again:

{
"title": "LOC-d7a06b60 Web logs",
"panels": [
 {"title":"Requests over time","chart_type":"line","data_view":"Kibana Sample Data Logs","metrics":[{"agg":"count","field":null,"label":"Requests"}],"group_by":[{"field":"timestamp","kind":"date_histogram","limit":10}]},
 {"title":"Requests by response code","chart_type":"bar","data_view":"Kibana Sample Data Logs","metrics":[{"agg":"count","field":null,"label":"Requests"}],"group_by":[{"field":"response.code","kind":"terms","limit":10}]}]
}

Now call.

